// Template for Config/Secrets.xcconfig, which is gitignored.
//
// Copy this file to Config/Secrets.xcconfig and fill in the real values from the
// Supabase dashboard (Project Settings -> API), or via:
//   supabase projects api-keys --project-ref ztdggewgqaoaixjhttct
//
// These are dev-project credentials. The publishable key is designed to be shipped
// in a client and is constrained by Row Level Security. Never put the service role
// key here: it bypasses RLS entirely and must stay server-side.
//
// Only the host is stored, not the full URL: xcconfig treats "//" as the start of a
// comment, so "https://..." would be silently truncated. The scheme is prepended in
// Swift when the client is constructed.

SUPABASE_API_HOST = your-project-ref.supabase.co
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY = sb_publishable_replace_me
